# attack — success
#
# The attack verb carried through: forced past the dice, the first blow lands, and the fight opens
# on a man already marked.
#
# Reached in 12/12 of the sampled location ids (see --verb-probe). --location-type and
# --location-id decide the whole scene, so this does not depend on world generation; --npc-static
# pins people to one room; --observe-only pins the phase to one object, which is why the keyword is
# clicked by index (which word the prose highlights is not something a test can know).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The fight is HELD here rather than entered, which is the whole point of the first-blow layer: the
# chips are the only account the player gets of what the swing did, and the fight screen paints over
# the narration carrying them. `state` reports fight-held=yes for a script that presses nothing.
expect SUCCESS

# What makes this an attack test rather than an any-verb test: every verb alike can enter a fight
# (a failed action under threat does), so only this can tell them apart.
expect-verb attack

# The blow itself — prefix only, since which skill was drawn and what it broke move with the body.
expect First blow:
# What the blow taught. Attack declares no lesson of its own: it teaches the modus mentis behind
# whichever fighting skill the blow drew, so this chip is the only proof the grant happened at all.
expect Modus mentis
# The outcome TYPES, asserted by their stable ids rather than by chip wording. `expect <chip>`
# proves what the player was told; this proves what actually ran. See --outcome-audit.
expect-outcome first_blow
expect-outcome fight_trigger

# And only now the fight, on the press that closes the segment.
click button
wait mode Fighting 60
quit
